","filename":"fission-ss.png"},{"key":"cf004377c68dbc428ecaf09f19db1493","url":"https://inspirehep.net/files/cf004377c68dbc428ecaf09f19db1493","source":"arxiv","caption":"The NR background spectrum from simulation.","filename":"nr-spectrum.png"},{"key":"3dc8fb46b521d776966657fe5fc319a7","url":"https://inspirehep.net/files/3dc8fb46b521d776966657fe5fc319a7","source":"arxiv","caption":"Distribution of NR background events in the target from simulation.","filename":"distribution-nr.png"},{"key":"cf1b1157626b8bcf13c6fcfaec0344da","url":"https://inspirehep.net/files/cf1b1157626b8bcf13c6fcfaec0344da","source":"arxiv","caption":"NR events selection efficiency as a function of nuclear recoil energy in various runs of the PandaX-II.","filename":"NReff.png"},{"key":"9dce27c5dc5a96c20c20539897d17cb1","url":"https://inspirehep.net/files/9dce27c5dc5a96c20c20539897d17cb1","source":"arxiv","caption":"Event rate from coherent neutrino-nucleus scattering in xenon. The neutrio sources include solar neutrinos ($\\rm ^{8}B$, $hep$, $\\rm ^{7}Be$, CNO neutrinos, $pp$ chains), atmospheric neutrinos ($\\nu_{e}$, $\\bar{\\nu}_{e}$, $\\nu_{\\mu}$, $\\bar{\\nu}_{\\mu}$) and diffuse supernovae (${\\rm T}_{\\nu_{e}}$=3~MeV, ${\\rm T}_{\\bar{\\nu}_{e}}$=5~MeV, ${\\rm T}_{\\nu_{x}}$=8~MeV).","filename":"neutrinoNR.png"},{"key":"9caf3b8ab96cd8e352f4bac4f2921a53","url":"https://inspirehep.net/files/9caf3b8ab96cd8e352f4bac4f2921a53","source":"arxiv","caption":"PandaX-4T sensitivity (at $90\\%$ C.L.) to WIMP-nucleon recoil events with an exposure of 5.6~ton-year. We compare the result with other leading experiments: LUX~\\cite{lux2017}, XENON1T~\\cite{xenon2017}, PandaX-II~\\cite{tan2016,cui2017}.","filename":"sensitivity_SI_new.png"},{"key":"60aa172808c04d50dab314c043ac3c64","url":"https://inspirehep.net/files/60aa172808c04d50dab314c043ac3c64","source":"arxiv","caption":"PandaX-4T sensitivity (at $90\\%$ C.L.) to WIMP-nucleon recoil for spin-dependent interaction, upper: proton-only, lower: neutron-only. We compare the results with the world data: LUX~\\cite{luxSD}, XENON100~\\cite{xenonSD}, PandaX-II~\\cite{fu2016}, CMS~\\cite{monojetcms}, ATLAS~\\cite{monojetatlas}, PICO~\\cite{pico1,pico2}, IceCube~\\cite{icecube} and Super-K~\\cite{superk}.","filename":"sensitivity_SDneutron_new.png"},{"key":"305539327ce9e49f5f3c877ceb387c4a","url":"https://inspirehep.net/files/305539327ce9e49f5f3c877ceb387c4a","source":"arxiv","caption":"PandaX-4T sensitivity (at $90\\%$ C.L.) to WIMP-nucleon recoil for spin-dependent interaction, upper: proton-only, lower: neutron-only. We compare the results with the world data: LUX~\\cite{luxSD}, XENON100~\\cite{xenonSD}, PandaX-II~\\cite{fu2016}, CMS~\\cite{monojetcms}, ATLAS~\\cite{monojetatlas}, PICO~\\cite{pico1,pico2}, IceCube~\\cite{icecube} and Super-K~\\cite{superk}.","filename":"sensitivity_SDproton_new.png"}],"license":[{"url":"http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/","license":"arXiv nonexclusive-distrib 1.0","material":"preprint"}],"texkeys":["PandaX:2018wtu","Zhang:2018xdp"],"citeable":true,"imprints":[{"date":"2018-08-17"}],"keywords":[{"value":"dark matter","source":"author"},{"value":"WIMPs","source":"author"},{"value":"direct detection","source":"author"},{"value":"xenon","source":"author"},{"value":"dark matter: direct detection","schema":"INSPIRE"},{"value":"electron: recoil","schema":"INSPIRE"},{"value":"nucleus: recoil","schema":"INSPIRE"},{"value":"background","schema":"INSPIRE"},{"value":"sensitivity","schema":"INSPIRE"},{"value":"numerical calculations","schema":"INSPIRE"},{"value":"deep underground detector","schema":"INSPIRE"}],"refereed":true,"abstracts":[{"value":"The PandaX-4T experiment, a 4-ton scale dark matter direct detection experiment, is being planned at the China Jinping Un- derground Laboratory. In this paper we present a simulation study of the expected background in this experiment. In a 2.8-ton fiducial mass and the signal region between 1–10 keV electron equivalent energy, the total electron recoil background is found to be 4:9 × 10$^{−5}$ kg$^{−1}$d$^{−1}$keV$^{−1}$. The nuclear recoil background in the same region is 2:8 × 10$^{−7}$ kg$^{−1}$d$^{−1}$keV$^{−1}$. With an exposure of 5.6 ton-years, the sensitivity of PandaX-4T could reach a minimum spin-independent dark matter-nucleon cross section of 6 × 10$^{−48}$ cm$^{2}$ at a dark matter mass of 40 GeV/c$^{2}$.","source":"Springer"},{"value":"The PandaX-4T experiment, a four-ton scale dark matter direct detection experiment, is being planned at the China Jinping Underground Laboratory. In this paper we present a simulation study of the expected background in this experiment. In a 2.8-ton fiducial mass and the signal region between 1 to 10 keV electron equivalent energy, the total electron recoil background is found to be 4.9x10^{-5} /(kg day keV). The nuclear recoil background in the same region is 2.8x10^{-7}/(kg day keV). With an exposure of 5.6 ton-years, the sensitivity of PandaX-4T could reach a minimum spin-independent dark matter-nucleon cross section of 6x10^{-48} cm^{2} at a dark matter mass of 40 GeV/c^{2}.","source":"arXiv"}],"references":[{"record":{"$ref":"https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/145023"},"reference":{"label":"1","authors":[{"full_name":"Faber, S.M."},{"full_name":"Gallagher, J.S."}],"publication_info":{"year":1979,"artid":"135","page_start":"135","journal_title":"Ann.Rev.Astron.Astrophys.","journal_volume":"17"}},"curated_relation":false},{"record":{"$ref":"https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/199948"},"reference":{"label":"2","authors":[{"full_name":"Blumenthal, G.R."},{"full_name":"Faber, S."},{"full_name":"Primack, J.R."},{"full_name":"Rees, M.J."}],"publication_info":{"year":1984,"page_end":"525","page_start":"517","journal_title":"Nature","journal_volume":"311"}},"curated_relation":false},{"record":{"$ref":"https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/1343079"},"reference":{"misc":["(Planck Collaboration)"],"label":"3","authors":[{"full_name":"Ade, P.A.R."}],"pub